    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9179A\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, relating to prohibiting insurance\ndiscrimination on the basis of an insured's marital status following the\ndeath of the insured's spouse\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nProhibits insurance discrimination on the basis of an insured's marital\nstatus following the death of the insured's spouse\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 2607 of the insurance law of subpart D of part\nJ of chapter 57 of the laws of 2019, to prohibit insurance companies\nfrom discriminating against applicants or policyholders based on sex,\nmarital status, or sexual stereotyping. Insurers cannot refuse to issue,\ncancel, decline to renew, limit coverage, or increase rates solely\nbecause someone became widowed. The protections extend to all types of\ninsurance, including property, casualty, homeowner's, renter's, and\nautomobile insurance.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation will prohibit insurance companies from discriminating\nagainst individuals based on their marital status following the death of\na spouse. Commonly referred to as the \"widow penalty,\" such practices\nunfairly increase premiums, limit coverage, or refuse renewal for\nwidowed policyholders. This legislation ensures that surviving spouses\nhave equitable access to insurance coverage, including property, casual-\nty, homeowner's, renter's, and automobile insurance, thereby protecting\nvulnerable households from financial hardship and promoting fairness in\nthe insurance market.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first day of January next succeeding\nthe date on which it shall have become a law and shall apply to any\npolicy issued, delivered, renewed, and/or modified on or after the\neffective date of this act.\n",
